<title>USA: Royce Labs gets OK for Pentazocine/Naloxone.</title>
<headline>Royce Labs gets OK for Pentazocine/Naloxone.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royce Laboratories Inc said Wendesday it had received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for its abbreviated new drug application (ANDA) for Pentazocine and Naloxone Hydrochlorides Tablets.</p>
<p>Pentazocine with Naloxone is the generic equivalent of Talwin NX, a narcotic pain reliever made by Sanofi's Sanofi Winthrop division.</p>
